# antigravity-seo-port

Tier-4 SEO analysis toolkit — 25 skills and 18 specialist subagent skills, ported from [AgriciDaniel/claude-seo](https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo).

## How to use

Skills are discovered automatically. Invoke any of them by name (or via Antigravity's skill picker):

- `seo-audit` — full site audit
- `seo-page` — single page analysis
- `seo-schema` — JSON-LD schema detection + validation
- `seo-geo` — GEO/generative engine optimization
- …and 20 more (run `ls ~/.gemini/antigravity-seo-port/skills/` for the full list)

Specialist subagent skills are suffixed `-agent` where they would have collided with a same-named skill.

## Tool-name mapping (Claude Code → Antigravity)

Upstream skills reference Claude Code tool names. If a skill says:

| Claude Code | Antigravity equivalent |
|---|---|
| `Read` | `view_file` |
| `Write` | `write_to_file` |
| `Edit` | `replace_file_content` / `multi_replace_file_content` |
| `Bash` | `run_command` |
| `Grep` | `grep_search` |
| `WebFetch` | `read_url_content` |
| `WebSearch` | `search_web` |
| `Task` (subagent) | `invoke_subagent` |

## Extension assets

- `scripts/` — Python helpers used by skills (`fetch_page.py`, etc.). Resolved at absolute paths inside skill bodies.
- `schema/`, `pdf/`, `data/` — JSON-LD templates, guides, sample data.
- `hooks/validate-schema.py` + `hooks/hooks.json` — `PostToolUse` hook that validates JSON-LD on Edit/Write.
- `.venv/` — Python virtual environment for scripts.
- `.env` — credentials for script-only extensions (Bing, Profound, SE Ranking). Owner-tagged; mode 0600.

